# Security (when the task may affect trust boundaries)

Treat these as **security-relevant**: auth (Better Auth, sessions, OAuth), env/secrets, API routes and proxies, database queries, file upload, CORS, tokens, webhooks, user input rendered or stored, and anything that crosses the Webflow Designer iframe ↔ Tower server boundary.

## Before finishing security-relevant work

- **Secrets**: never commit `.env`, API keys, or tokens; use env vars and existing config patterns only.
- **Input**: validate and normalize untrusted input at boundaries; do not trust client/extension payloads on the server.
- **AuthZ**: enforce authorization on the server for every sensitive action; do not rely on UI hiding alone.
- **Output**: avoid leaking stack traces, internal IDs, or secrets in errors shown to users.
- **Dependencies**: prefer existing crypto/auth libraries; do not roll custom crypto or token formats.
- **OWASP basics**: guard injection (SQL/NoSQL/command), XSS (escape or framework defaults), SSRF on outbound fetches, and open redirects on OAuth/callback URLs.

If unsure, state assumptions and choose the stricter default. Do not ship “we can harden later” shortcuts on auth or data handling.
